doc:sch-1-sec-154zw a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154ZW Contents of variation or revocation of approval" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A variation or revocation made under section 154ZV must specify the details of the variation or revocation, including: (a) the day on which the decision to make the variation or revocation was made; and (b) the day on which the variation or revocation takes effect; and (c) in the case of a variation that changes or removes the date on which the approval ceases to be in force—that change or removal; and (d) in the case of a variation that changes or removes conditions to which the approval is subject—that change or removal." ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-fair-go-for-consumers-and-small-business-act-sch-1-sec-154zx a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154ZX Notice of decision on application for variation or revocation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-154zx ;
    values:originalText "of approval (1) If the Minister: (a) decides to vary or revoke a designated complainant’s approval; or (b) in a case where a designated complainant has applied for a variation or revocation of its approval—decides not to vary or revoke the approval; the Minister must give the designated complainant, as soon as practicable: (c) notice of the decision; and  Designated complaints  Schedule 1  No. 16, 2024 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Fair Go for Consumers and Small Business) Act 2024 (d) if the decision is to vary or revoke the approval—a copy of the variation or revocation. (2) As soon as practicable after varying or revoking the approval, the Minister: (a) must give a copy of the notice of the decision to the Commission; and (b) in the case of a revocation—must publish that fact on the Department’s website; and (c) in the case of a variation that changes or removes conditions to which the approval is subject—may publish details of that change or removal on the Department’s website." ;
    skos:definition "of approval (1) If the Minister: (a) decides to vary or revoke a designated complainant’s approval; or (b) in a case where a designated complainant has applied for a variation or revocation of its approval—decides not to vary or revoke the approval; the Minister must give the designated complainant, as soon as practicable: (c) notice of the decision; and  Designated complaints  Schedule 1  No. 16, 2024 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Fair Go for Consumers and Small Business) Act 2024 (d) if the decision is to vary or revoke the approval—a copy of the variation or revocation. (2) As soon as practicable after varying or revoking the approval, the Minister: (a) must give a copy of the notice of the decision to the Commission; and (b) in the case of a revocation—must publish that fact on the Department’s website; and (c) in the case of a variation that changes or removes conditions to which the approval is subject—may publish details of that change or removal on the Department’s website."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a62b261375826e253ae4533a10421dcf355fcd9b9b4d84785864a600d6df121" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-fair-go-for-consumers-and-small-business-act-sch-1-sec-154zx-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-fair-go-for-consumers-and-small-business-act-sch-1-sec-154zx-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
